You're right about polypiling.  Be warned, though, it can have bad
side-effects!
Cursed Genocide scrolls, instead of wiping a monster type out,
_surround_ you with monsters of that type.  A good way to get
intrinsics...if you're tough enough to win the fight, of course.
The Platinum Yendorian Express Card is the Tourist quest item--when
#invoked, it acts like a scroll of charging (like a blessed scroll of
charging when blessed).  This makes it a pretty powerful item, but of
course this helps balance out the fact that Tourists are generally
pretty wimpy characters.
It's not so much that _using_ PYEC is an abuse, but some (including
myself) consider _wishing_ for a PYEC (the only way that non-tourists
can obtain it) to be a no-no.  It detracts from the uniqueness of the
Tourist class.  (Maybe...hope hope...wishing for quest artifacts will
be disallowed in future versions...)



